# Livewire Security
- Treat every public property as client-writable: mark ids, foreign keys, prices, flags, and any server-owned state `#[Locked]`.
- Treat every public method as a routable endpoint: authorize inside each action (`$this->authorize()`, Gate, policy) — visibility in the view is not protection.
- Validate all bound input before use or persistence; never mass-assign raw public properties into models.
- Never trust `mount()` arguments resolved from the route or query string — authorize the resolved resource and scope lookups to the authenticated user/tenant.
- File uploads: use `WithFileUploads`, validate mimes/size/dimensions in rules, and expose previews only via `temporaryUrl()` — never raw temp paths.
- Do not store secrets, tokens, or other users' data in public properties — they serialize into the page payload.
- Re-check authorization in every action that mutates state, not only in `mount()` — component state outlives the initial request.
- Rate-limit expensive or abusable actions (login, search, messaging) with the framework rate limiter.
